    "statement": "histogram_quantile(0.99) returns a value inside (100, 250] ms only if at least ~1% of the spans in the 2 m rate window were slower than 100 ms. Linear interpolation inside the bucket means the exact value (227.5 vs 244.8) reflects bucket mass, not a measured latency.",
    "single_hop_expectation_ms": "cartservice baseline p99 ~5-8 ms + one 50 ms egress delay would land in (50, 100] ms if the delay were applied once per request. Observing p99 > 100 ms therefore requires >=1% of spans to carry more than ~one delayed hop or additional queueing/retry/client-span effects. This is a lower-bound argument, not an identification of the mechanism.",
    "mean_latency_not_available": true
  },
