  "measurement_definition_issues_from_code": [
    "Query regex span_name=~\"(?i).*<service>.*\" matches any span whose NAME contains the service string, with no span_kind filter; callers' client spans and callee server spans are merged.",
    "sum by (le) merges all matching operations into a single mixture histogram.",
    "tc filter 'u32 match ip protocol 6' delays ALL TCP egress from the cart container (gRPC replies, Redis requests, telemetry export), not only application replies.",
    "Active-phase analysis window (110 s) and rate(...[2m]) both extend beyond the 30 s intervention."
  ],
  "conclusion": "Not resolvable from saved data. Compounded multi-hop egress delay is consistent with p99 > 100 ms but 2 x 50 ms = ~100 ms still leaves part of the 227-245 ms bucket-interpolated value unexplained; queueing, retries, mixed client/server span aggregation and bucket interpolation are not excluded. No per-request, per-hop or trace data were saved, so no mechanism is claimed."
